E4 Monitor for Z80 Micro
When allowing Background Interrupts while in Shadow Monitor, note that the
interrupts cannot execute code in the range 0000-07ff, and similarly DMA
started before entry to the Shadow Monitor will not read correct addresses
from the 0000-07ff address range.  The exception to this is the interrupt
vectors themselves, when enabled, ie addresses 0038-003F if RST7 used.  If
NMI is enabled, ranges 0066-00FF and 0800-FFFF may be accessed by the NMI
routine.

nmi	66	ff
rst0	0	7
rst1	8	f
rst2	10	17
rst3	18	1f
rst4	20	27
rst5	28	2f
rst6	30	37
rst7	38	3f
